    Takes as input a string encoded with the encode_shift function, which shifts every character by 5 positions within the lowercase English alphabet ('a'–'z'), wrapping around from 'z' to 'a'. 
    Assumes the input string contains only lowercase English letters ('a'–'z'). 
    Returns the decoded string by reversing the 5-position shift for each character.
