    - The parity check is performed on the binary representation of the absolute value of the input integer.
    - Zero (0) is considered to have even parity since it has zero 1 bits.

    Examples:
    >>> check_Even_Parity(5)  # binary 101 has two 1s, even parity
    True
    >>> check_Even_Parity(7)  # binary 111 has three 1s, odd parity
    False
    >>> check_Even_Parity(0)  # binary 0 has zero 1s, even parity
    True
    """
